{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg2HoGpG2q5KcqxDafgSX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Items now have an optional `notes` text field, with a `--notes` flag on `add`. The test suite passes (14 tests).\n\n**What changed**\n- `shelvanta/items.py`: `Item` gets `notes: str = \"\"`. It is saved in the JSON file like the other fields.\n- `shelvanta/storage.py`: re-adding an existing SKU keeps its notes unless new notes are given.\n- `shelvanta/cli.py`: `add` accepts `--notes`.\n- Tests cover the default, the CLI flag, the save/load round trip, old rows without `notes` loading as empty, and keeping notes on re-add.\n\n**Choices I made**\n- **No migration.** Storage is a JSON file, not a database. `migrations/001_init.sql` is reserved for a future backend, and CLAUDE.md says to add a migration only when asked. If you want the SQL schema updated too, say so and I'll add a new numbered migration file.\n- **`list` does not show notes.** I kept the output format unchanged. Say if you want a notes column.\n- **Notes can't be cleared on re-add.** An empty `--notes` means \"keep existing notes\". Clearing would need a separate command or flag.\n\n**Checks**\n- The reviewer agent reported PASS. It could not run `git diff`, so I checked `git status` myself. Only the five intended files are modified. Nothing under \"Do not touch\" changed.\n- The reviewer also raised a pre-existing risk: an unknown key in the JSON file would crash `load` with a `TypeError` that `main()` does not catch. I did not change this.\n- A cleanup command to delete the `__pycache__` directories from my test run was blocked, so those directories remain. They are untracked and harmless. Delete them with `rm -rf tests/__pycache__ shelvanta/__pycache__` if you want a clean tree."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":562,"cache_read_input_token